  "continuation_revision_rationale": {
    "cpu:hybench_tp": "A16 with 8 clients reached 1.666/2 cores; the v16 fresh run with 12 clients reached only 1.523 cores (warm-up 1.766), still below the 1.8-core bottleneck threshold, so use 16 clients consistently for A16 and both B4 repeats.",
    "cpu:tpcc": "A17 baseline was 1.72 cores against a 1.8-core threshold; raise terminals from 60 to 80.",
    "memory:job": "The v16 attempt 3 fresh baseline crashed PostgreSQL under 16 workers and work_mem=160MB at 768 MiB. Historical 12-worker/144MB real JOB replays completed with about 0.652 GiB measured memory, which remains above 90% of the current 0.693-GiB usable capacity, so use that less extreme bottleneck load for A14 recovery.",
    "io:hybench_xp": "A18 baseline was 4.09 MiB/s against a 4.59-MiB/s threshold; raise AP clients from 24 to 28 without overshooting the feasible 5-10% drop interval."
  },
